                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesRelationToIndexTheory"} Relation to index theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_trace_formulas"} Relation to trace formulas
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Where a system of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            is specified by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hermitean+operator"} hermitean operator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
                – the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
          %p
            a system of
            %em supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            has
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Hilbert+space"} super Hilbert space
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
            %li
              %p
                an odd
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℋ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercharge"} supercharge
            %li
              %p
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \circ D = H
                is the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
          %p
            If we regard the Hamiltonian as the generator of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+Lie+algebra"} Poincare Lie algebra
            in one dimension – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+Lie+algebra"} super translation Lie algebra
            –, then the graded commutator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,D] = 2 H
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            extension to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} super Poincaré Lie algebra
            in super-dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1|1)
          %p
            The data of a system of supersymmetric quantum mechanics may also be formalized in terms of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triple"} spectral triple
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToSpinningParticles Relation to spinning particles
          %p
            A simple but often underappreciated fact is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline+theory"} worldline theory
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particle"} spinning particle
            is supersymmetric, and hence is supersymmetric quantum mechanics,
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldline"} worldline
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            in the world. See at
            = succeed "for" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "spinning+particle#WorldlineSupersymmetry"} spinning particle – Worldline supersymmetry
          %p Of course the bulk of the literature considers non-relativistic supersymmetric quantum mechanics. That is much less relevant in nature.
          %h3#RelationToIndexTheory Relation to index theory
          %p
            Another fairly simple but very deep fact is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of a supersymmetric
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanical+system"} quantum mechanical system
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertrace"} supertrace
            of its propagator, is equivalently what in mathematics (in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the supercharge regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operator"} Fredholm operator
            %a{:href => "#ReferencesRelationToIndexTheory"} below
            for more on this.
          %p
            This relation is at the heart of a deep and ubiquituous role that supersymmetric quantum mechanics plays in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            and related topics (and vice versa). For a general abstract discussion of why there is such a relation see also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "super+algebra#AbstractIdea"} super algebra – Abstract idea
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+line+2-bundle"} super line 2-bundle
          %h3#relation_to_morse_theory Relation to Morse theory
          %p
            For the moment see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesRelationToMorseTheory"} below
          %h3#RelationToSuperstrings Relation to superstrings
          %p
            Supersymmetric quantum mechanics was introduced or at least became famous with (
            %a{:href => "#Wittem82"}> Witten 82
            ). As explained at the end of (
            %a{:href => "#Witten85"}> Witten 85
            ),
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Witten
            had come to consider this while looking at the point particle limit of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} 2-spectral triple
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Schreiber04"} Schreiber 04
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
            translates to Witten’s interpretation of the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            as what is now known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (see there for more).
          %p
            One way to make this rigorously precise would be to realize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac-Ramond+operator"} Dirac-Ramond operator
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            as an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator+on+smooth+loop+space"} Dirac operator on smooth loop space
            (the string’s
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wheeler+superspace"} Wheeler superspace
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Witten87b"} Witten 87b
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+theory"} Morse theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C1%29-dimensional+Euclidean+field+theories+and+K-theory"} (1,1)-dimensional Euclidean field theories and K-theory
          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Tong"}> David Tong
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetric Quantum Mechanics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/susyqm.html"} webpage
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/susy/susyqm.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A fairly comprehensive survey and discussion of supersymmetric quantum mechanics as such, with emphasis on its relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+geometry"} spectral geometry
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"}> noncommutative geometry
            ”) is in
          %ul
            %li#FGR96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              , Oiver Grandjean,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Recknagel"} Andreas Recknagel
              = succeed "," do
                %em Supersymmetric quantum theory and (non-commutative) differential geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9612205"} arXiv:hep-th/9612205
          %p
            and with more emphasis on the relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triples"}> 2-spectral triples
            ):
          %ul
            %li#FGR97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              , Oliver Grandjean,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Recknagel"} Andreas Recknagel
              %em Supersymmetric quantum theory, non-commutative geometry, and gravitation
              Lecture Notes Les Houches (1995) (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9706132"}> arXiv:hep-th/9706132
              ).
          %p Further survey;
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Fred Cooper, Avinash Khare, Uday Sukhatme,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and Quantum Mechanics
                %strong 251
                (1995) 267-385 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9405029"}> arXiv:hep-th/9405029
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                V. P. Berezovoj,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+J.+Nurmagambetov"} Alexei J. Nurmagambetov
                %em Applied Supersymmetry
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.02081"}> arXiv:2507.02081
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            in the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+over+supermanifolds"}> integration over supermanifolds
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/picture+changing+operators"} picture changing operators
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Castellani"}> Leonardo Castellani
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Catenacci"} Roberto Catenacci
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Grassi"} Pietro Grassi
              = succeed "," do
                %em Super Quantum Mechanics in the Integral Form Formalism
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.04704"} arXiv:1706.04704
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Nick Dorey, Boan Zhao,
                %em Supersymmetric quantum mechanics and growth of sheaf cohomology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.11834"}> arXiv:2209.11834
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Vyacheslav P. Spiridonov,
                %em Variations of supersymmetric quantum mechanics and superconformal indices
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.10609"}> arXiv:2404.10609
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Ivan G. Avramidi:
                %em On Zero Energy States in SUSY Quantum Mechanics on Manifolds
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.09040"}> arXiv:2502.09040
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiclassical+approximation"} semiclassical approximation
          %ul
            %li
              Asim Gangopadhaya, Jonathan Bougie, Constantin Rasinariu:
              %em Recent Advances in Semiclassical Methods Inspired by Supersymmetric Quantum Mechanics
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.15424"}> arXiv:2408.15424
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToMorseTheory Relation to Morse theory and string theory
          %p Supersymmetric quantum mechanics gained attention with the work
          %ul
            %li#Witten82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Supersymmetry and Morse theory
              J. Differential Geom.
              %strong 17
              4 (1982) 661-692. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214437492"}> euclid:jdg/1214437492
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cimat.mx/~gil/docencia/2012/teoria_de_morse/witten_supersymmetry_and_morse_theory.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/176416"} spire:176416
          %p
            which showed that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+theory"} Morse theory
            may be equivalently interpreted as the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            in supersymmetric quantum mechanics, and which was part of what gained Witten the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://159.226.47.99:8080/general/prize/medal/1990.htm"} Fields medal 1990
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superparticles"} superparticles
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            are considered and the supersymmetric ground states are shown to be given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morse+theory"} Morse theory
            of the deformation function.
          %p For a survey of the relation to Morse theory see for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%C3%A1bor+Pete"}> Gábor Pete
                , section 2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Morse theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.bme.hu/~gabor/morse.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Rohit Jain,
                %em Supersymmetric Schrödinger operators with applications to Morse theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/rjain/SUSY.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            This deformed supersymmetric quantum mechanics arises as the point-particle limit of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            regarded as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loop+space"} smooth loop space
            (the string’s
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wheeler+superspace"} Wheeler superspace
          %ul
            %li#Witten85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              , p. 92-94 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Global anomalies in string theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/conferences/965785?ui-citation-summary=true"} Symposium on Anomalies, Geometry, Topology
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/WittenGlobalAnomaliesInStringTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/214913"} spire:214913
          %p and then in
          %ul
            %li#Witten87b
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Index Of The Dirac Operator In Loop Space
              = succeed "," do
                %em Elliptic Curves and Modular Forms in Algebraic Topology
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 1326
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0078045"} doi:10.1007/BFb0078045
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/245523"} spire
          %p
            The relation between the 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} SCFT
            describing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            and this deformed supersymmetric quantum mechanics on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+loop+space"} smooth loop space
            has been further explored in
          %ul
            %li#Schreiber04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On deformations of 2d SCFTs
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0401175"} arXiv:hep-th/0401175
          %p
            Further discussion of supersymmetric quantum mechanics in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
          %p
            On supersymmetric quantum mechanics of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BFSS+matrix+model"} BFSS matrix model
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model"} BMN matrix model
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+Calabi-Yau+5-folds"} M-theory on Calabi-Yau 5-folds
            in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Haupt"}> Alexander Haupt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kellogg+Stelle"} Kellogg Stelle
              = succeed "," do
                %em M-theory on Calabi-Yau Five-Folds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0810.2685"} arXiv:0810.2685
          %h3#ReferencesRelationToIndexTheory Relation to index theory
          %p
            The relation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of supersymmetric quantum mechanics to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
            was suggested in unpublished work of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
            and formulated in
          %ul#Getzler86
            %li#AlvarezGaume83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alvarez-Gaum%C3%A9"}> Luis Alvarez-Gaumé
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and the Atiyah-Singer index theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1103940278"} Euclid
            %li#Getzler83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Pseudodifferential operators on supermanifolds and the Atiyah-Singer index theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~getzler/Papers/1103940796.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Quillen"}> D. Quillen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Superconnections and the Chern character
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0040-9383%2885%2990047-3"} doi
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"}> Varghese Mathai
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"} Daniel Quillen
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Superconnections, Thom classes, and equivariant differential forms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A short proof of the Atiyah-Singer index theorem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~getzler/Papers/local.pdf"} pdf
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D.+Quillen"}> D. Quillen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Superconnection character forms and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+transform"} Cayley transform
          %h3#relation_to_trace_formulas Relation to trace formulas
          %p
            Relation to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Selberg+trace+formula"} Selberg trace formula
            and other trace formulas:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Changha+Choi"}> Changha Choi
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leon+A.+Takhtajan"} Leon A. Takhtajan
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Supersymmetry and trace formulas I. Compact Lie groups
                %strong 2024
                26 (2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.07942"}> arXiv:2112.07942
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP06(2024)026"} doi:10.1007/JHEP06(2024)026
            %li
              %p
